# The Emscripten version the WebAssembly SDL libraries are compiled with, one line per .NET
# version KappaDuck.Khaos.Native ships WebAssembly SDL for: NET<major>=<Emscripten version>.
#
# A WebAssembly build relinks dotnet.native.wasm with SDL's static .a libraries, and the
# wasm-tools workload picks its Emscripten from the game's target framework, not from the SDK:
# SDK 11 links a net11.0 game with Emscripten 6.0.3 and a net10.0 game with 3.1.56
# (wasm-tools-net10). Mixing versions fails at link time, so each .NET version gets its own
# set of .a files in the package (wasm/<tfm>/), built with that version's Emscripten.
#
# The workload records its version in
# packs/Microsoft.NET.Runtime.Emscripten.<x>.Sdk.<rid>/<version>/tools/emscripten/emscripten-version.txt;
# the pack's folder name is not enough (the 6.0.2 pack holds 6.0.3).
#
# Pinned by hand on purpose: an SDK update that moves Emscripten shows up as a diff of this
# file, and build-wasm.sh stops when the installed workload has another version.
#
# When a new .NET arrives: add the .NET with its previews, keep NET11 while Khaos supports it.
# On new .NET, NET11 needs `dotnet workload install wasm-tools-net11`.
NET11=6.0.3
